course: dictionary
lesson: 5668
title: One word, many meanings: live
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Live is a small word with lots of jobs. Say it two ways. As a verb it rhymes with give: «Macaws live in the forests of Central and South America.» It means they have their home there. As an adjective it rhymes with five: live animals are alive, not dead.
explain: The clues around the word tell you its meaning. «Each person has one life on this earth; nobody else can live it for them.» Here live means to spend your life, the way you go through it. Ask yourself: what would fit in the sentence instead?
explain: Sometimes live means happening now, not recorded. A live show is on stage or on TV as it happens. A live wire is different: it carries electricity and is dangerous, so you must never touch it. Check the words near live to see which meaning is right.
explain: Live also shows up in stories and science. «They lived happily ever after» means they spent their lives happily. In science, living things grow, need food and water, and reproduce. «Moths live in» a sloth's fur, so they have their home there.
fact: Live rhymes with give when it is a verb: «They live here.»
fact: Live rhymes with five when it is an adjective: «live animals».
fact: «Live» can mean to be alive, to have your home somewhere, or to spend your life in a certain way.
fact: A live wire carries electricity and is dangerous. Never touch one.
fact: In science, living things grow, need food and water, and reproduce.
exercise: «Macaws live in the forests of Central and South America.» In this sentence, live means | To go on a long trip | To fly high above the trees | To sing very loudly | *To have their home there
exercise: Which meaning fits «a live show»? | A show with no sound | Happening long ago | A show made of wires | *Happening now, not recorded
exercise: A sign says «Never touch a live wire.» What does live mean here? | Recorded on a video | Very long and thin | Alive, like a worm | *Carrying electricity and dangerous
test: «Fish can live with an uneven fin from birth or injury.» In this sentence, live means | *To survive and carry on living | To be recorded for later | To have a home in a shop | To be very quiet
test: In «live animals», the word live is an adjective meaning | Recorded | *Alive, not dead | Happy | Dangerous
exam: «They lived happily ever after.» In this line, live means | *To spend your life in a certain way | Alive, not dead | Happening now | Carrying electricity
